+# Compact and Garage studio art pass - 2026-10-10
+
+Requirements: GS01 (one polished shared Compact asset), GS02 (cohesive automotive studio), GS03 (material/lighting quality and larger framing), GS04 (bounded asset/render cost), GL01-GL06/G01/V06/R01/Q01. The owner approves the proposed first Compact-and-studio slice after rejecting the prior view as visually unappealing and requesting an AAA quality ambition.
+
+The actual Compact now uses original smooth coachwork patches for its lower body, open wheel arches, crowned hood and rolled roof. Authoring remains editable native source, with normals, tangents and UVs. Body and arch overlays share the same projected atlas; hood body/accent surfaces share the corresponding hood coordinates. Original fictional identity, three-door silhouette, world metre scale and wheel locations/radii are retained. The small roof crown reaches 1.513 model metres; its cosmetic rollover support is raised from 1.49 to 1.515m. No handling/collision/rules/timing/score contracts change. Front/rear lamp construction, suspension, steering, independent rolling wheels and batching remain functional.
+
+Restrained satin paint and metal wheel materials replace maximum-roughness/specular-disabled paint. Smooth tire normals and an original UV tread finish improve close inspection. Fixed blue fender/door highlight cards are removed; actual body paint and roof crease materials follow their saved livery. A per-showroom glass material reflects the studio softboxes without changing the shared driving glass parameters. Painted body, glass, rubber and metal now read as distinct materials. The Compact material/geometry revision is shared with races; the other four vehicle models are not rebuilt in this slice.
+
+The Garage has a continuous 360-degree curved cove with quiet floor grain, warm key/cool fill/rim lighting, fixed cached studio sky radiance and a prepared soft ground shadow. The latter projects actual car mesh vertices under the fixed key direction, takes their convex hull and prepares 24 support planes once; it is a soft presentation approximation, not ray-traced or screen-space reflection/shadow reconstruction. There is no realtime studio shadow map, screenshot background, particle decoration or animated environment. Contact shading anchors each wheel. A coherent dark page background replaces the workshop showing between the Garage controls. The shared studio supports all five selected cars, while this task finishes only the Compact asset.
+
+Perspective FOV stays 38 degrees; Compact normal orbit distance changes from 7.1 to 5.5m before the existing elevation factor, for a larger car in the view. Other cars retain their distances. The prior full azimuth, 5-80 degree elevation, bounded pinch/wheel/trackpad zoom, toolbar and Reset view remain. The menu SubViewport uses 4x MSAA; driving retains its existing renderer, antialiasing, camera and physical scale. No new player-facing implementation labels or source badges.
+
+Fourteen compressed native ArrayMesh resources, **230924 bytes total**, are baked offline and reused as immutable geometry. Materials remain per instance. Runtime normally loads these resources; editable source regeneration is a diagnostic fallback for a missing asset. The source/bake regression compares every baked vertex/normal/tangent/UV/index array exactly against regeneration. The existing all-resources export includes the native meshes. Hashes and original-asset provenance: `game/assets/vehicles/compact_coachwork_v1/manifest.json`, its PROVENANCE.md and `licenses/ASSETS.md`. No external mesh, texture purchase or media service was used.
+
+Changed source files: `game/vehicle/car_visual.gd`, `compact_detail.gd`, `window_reflection.gdshader`; new `compact_coachwork.gd`, `compact_finish.gd`, `compact_tire.gdshader`; `game/ui/car_showroom.gd`, `garage_page.gd`; new `showroom_studio.gd`, `studio_sky.gdshader`, `studio_floor.gdshader`, `studio_contact.gdshader`, `studio_projection.gdshader`; new `game/tests/test_garage_studio.gd`, `bake_compact_coachwork.gd`, `capture_garage_studio.gd`; their generated UID sidecars, fourteen native meshes, manifest/provenance and this documentation/status/plan/license entry. The main game/app, other cars and canonical simulation were not edited. Unrelated concurrent audio/dust/menu/rating work is preserved and excluded from the [task-only text and binary Git checkpoint](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/scoped-change.patch).
+
+Actual commands use pinned Godot `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` through `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`, with normal Windows certificate/log access. Garage app fixtures disable the API URL and use isolated records/library/cloud roots. No player account or score writes.
+
+| Actual command | Actual outcome |
+| --- | --- |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/bake_compact_coachwork.gd` | Final **14 native meshes, 230924 bytes**; source-authored asset bake succeeds |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_studio.gd -Graphical` | Final **38 checks, zero failures**; finite/UV surfaces, independent world, original car identity, PBR paint, prepared studio shadow, exact source/bake parity for every mesh, geometry-preserving batching, wheels, live livery details, driving-glass isolation, six inspected studio views, layout and rotating render measurements |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_livery.gd -Graphical` | **115 checks, zero failures**; actual five-car selection, saved per-car colors, protected rotate gestures, picker/reset/save-failure behavior and race color application |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_garage_view_controls.gd -Graphical` | **59 checks, zero failures**, manual angle/pinch/wheel/trackpad/buttons/reset/bounds retained |
+| `-Action TestVehicleBatch` | **35 checks, zero failures**; all five cars retain exact source/batched triangles/bounds, independent wheels and lamps. Compact at that intermediate shared-roof-material point: 1203 nodes to 53 meshes; final independent roof material is 54 meshes, confirmed by final studio check |
+| `-Action TestSuspension` | **59 checks, zero failures**; wheel/suspension/ramp/roll presentation remains |
+| `-Action TestHandling` | **88 checks, zero failures**, including explicit offline exact-replay diagnostics; canonical implementation unchanged |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_headlights.gd` | **81 checks, zero failures**, functional headlights/rear lamps for all cars |
+| `-Action TestApp` | **99 checks, zero failures**, normal app/race/editor/PB flow |
+| `-Action CaptureCompactDetail` | **10 native views saved**; gameplay and front inspection reviewed |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/capture_garage_studio.gd -Graphical` | **Three actual app Garage captures**, 960x540, 1280x720, 1600x720 |
+| `-Action Import` | Final **exit 0** after correcting the studio reflection enum to the pinned API name |
+| `-Action TestScript -ScriptPath res://tests/test_script_parse.gd` | Broader scan initially failed in concurrent `finish_rating.gd` due native Node `owner` redefinition; a later scan failed in concurrent `test_track_rating_prompt.gd` because its referenced UI file was absent. These files were not altered to green this task; final retry **462 scripts, zero failures** after the independent edits settled |
+| `adb devices -l` | OnePlus Pad 2 OPD2403/f0ba474a attached; **no phone attached** |
+| Scoped whitespace/reverse Git checkpoint checks | Pass |
+
+Actual local performance is a measurement of the menu SubViewport on an RTX 3090/Compatibility desktop, not whole-app loading, phone pacing or a 60fps claim. Initial runtime source construction recorded **753.115ms**; baked construction recorded **130.159ms**, then final **170.085ms** with concurrent checks. These are individual observations rather than a controlled speed benchmark. Final rotating studio samples (90 measured frames after 30 warmup) report CPU median **0.695ms**, p95 **0.959ms**; GPU median **0.191ms**, p95 **1.630ms**. Final shared Compact: **41384 triangles, 54 batched meshes, 33050 UV vertices**. Device cost and any need for a lower detail mesh still require physical review.
+
+Initial visual review caught reversed cove winding, faceted cove normals, overlapping old fender highlight cards, a hood/body join and harsh self-shadowing. The final scene uses corrected smooth cove normals, continuous arches, a matched hood edge and prepared soft ground shadow. Two incorrect reflection-enum names were corrected using the existing pinned project/API. A concurrent orphan dust helper temporarily blocked an app capture; it was fixed by the independent work and no dust file was changed here. No test requirement was removed or weakened.
+
+Inspected evidence: [before](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/before/garage-1280.png), [actual Garage 1280](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/garage-app-1280.png), [actual Garage 960](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/garage-app-960.png), [copper paint](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/compact-copper-1280.png), [front close](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/compact-front-close-1280.png), [rear](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/compact-rear-1280.png), [race view](evidence/garage-studio-2026-10-10/gameplay.png). Standalone studio inspections omit the app navigation; the three garage-app captures use the actual app shell. All images are native renders, not generated posters.
+
+This is the first reviewable Compact/studio art pass toward the owner's quality target, not an automatic AAA acceptance claim. Remaining acceptance: owner close-up silhouette/material/studio review, real phone/tablet input and thermal/frame pacing, and deciding whether further asset detailing is needed before treating this as the bar for the other cars. Pattern/shape editing, cabin interior detailing, a full car collection art pass and Android export/install are outside this checkpoint. No physical-device test, APK export/install, full Validate, backend deployment or production action was performed for this task. Restart/rebuild the local client to use these changes. Prior broad menu-regression failures remain documented separately in GARAGE_LIVERY.md. The final full script scan passed 462 scripts after the unrelated rating work settled.
